\end{aligned}

Combining 

Eq. 61 and 

Eq. 62, and dividing through by m, we find:\ddot{\vector{r}} = -\frac{\mu_1}{r_1^3}\vector{r}_1 - \frac{\mu_2}{r_2^3}\vector{r}_2

Now we substitute for \ddot{\vector{r}} from 

